  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Zawad is a rare competitive programmer — he takes his studies seriously. One day, while studying in a library, he found a pattern PPP in a century old book. The pattern is a string of lowercase English letters, with length MMM. Since Zawad is a curious boy, he started experimenting with the pattern.\n\nIn one experiment, Zawad considers all 26N26^N26N strings with length NNN that contain only lowercase English letters. The strings are numbered 000 through 26N−126^N - 126N−1 in lexicographical order. For each valid iii, let CiC_iCi​ be the length of the longest prefix of PPP which is also a suffix of the iii-th of these strings (0≤Ci≤M0 \\le C_i \\le M0≤Ci​≤M).\n\nFor each integer kkk between 000 and MMM inclusive, let SkS_kSk​ denote the sum of all valid indices iii such that Ci=kC_i = kCi​=k. Zawad wants to know all these sums, but since they could be huge, it is enough to compute them modulo 998,244,353998,244,353998,244,353.\n\nSince Zawad is a bit busy at the library, he is asking for your help. Can you find the sums and earn Zawad's respect?",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤51 \\le T \\le 51≤T≤5",
      "1≤M≤1051 \\le M \\le 10^51≤M≤105",
      "M≤N≤106M \\le N \\le 10^6M≤N≤106",
      "PPP contains only lowercase English letters"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers MMM and NNN.\nThe second line contains a single string PPP with length MMM.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing M+1M+1M+1 space-separated integers S0,S1,…,SMS_0, S_1, \\ldots, S_MS0​,S1​,…,SM​ — the sums modulo 998,244,353998,244,353998,244,353.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
